From: Matthew Cather <matthew.cather@adtran.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 14:10:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: release rfkill config and assoc frame taxonomy

Stubbed rfkill init returns a sentinel instead of NULL, so callers that
own its config never release it. Station free skips the association
frame copy that the ubus binding keeps per station.

Both leaks are submitted upstream as openwrt/openwrt#25339. Drop this
patch when it lands.

Signed-off-by: Matthew Cather <matthew.cather@adtran.com>
---
 src/ap/sta_info.c    |    2 ++
 src/drivers/rfkill.h |    3 ++-
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/src/ap/sta_info.c
+++ b/src/ap/sta_info.c
@@ -375,6 +375,8 @@ void ap_free_sta(struct hostapd_data *ha
 	sta->probe_ie_taxonomy = NULL;
 	wpabuf_free(sta->assoc_ie_taxonomy);
 	sta->assoc_ie_taxonomy = NULL;
+	wpabuf_free(sta->assoc_frame_taxonomy);
+	sta->assoc_frame_taxonomy = NULL;
 #endif /* CONFIG_TAXONOMY */
 
 	ht40_intolerant_remove(hapd->iface, sta);
--- a/src/drivers/rfkill.h
+++ b/src/drivers/rfkill.h
@@ -25,7 +25,8 @@ int rfkill_is_blocked(struct rfkill_data
 #else
 static inline struct rfkill_data * rfkill_init(struct rfkill_config *cfg)
 {
-	return (void *) 1;
+	/* callers release the config only on a NULL return */
+	return NULL;
 }
 
 static inline void rfkill_deinit(struct rfkill_data *rfkill)
